WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.980
Vroom, vroom, vroom-r-room...

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.070
All day, every day, happy vroom-vroom...

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.610
Vroom-vroom at ten thousand horsepow—

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.240
Hey!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.660
Isn't that...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.090
G-Good morning!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.350
Huh?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.020
Huh?

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.290
So as you can see,

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.550
we’ll be going on a special extracurricular summer camp in two weeks.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:32.300
The girls will be going to Shikine Island, and the boys to Mt. Takao.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:39.560
Once we arrive, you'll be working in groups.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.480
Send me a form with your group members and leader by next Monday.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.610
Groups should be around 4-5 members, including the leader.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.030
<i>She's the girl I saw this morning, right?</i>

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:50.990
Groups should be around 4-5 members, including the leader.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.830
Let's dig in!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.880
Wow, your lunch looks amazing, Himawari!

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.340
It looks delicious!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:14.300
Uh... My mom was really happy when I told her I was gonna come to school...

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.100
She got even happier when I said I'd made friends...

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.270
She said I should share it with you...

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.020
Hurray!

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.810
Thanks a lot!

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.360
I'll take you on your offer.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.770
It looks yummy!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:30.280
It's great!

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.570
Yeah, it's fantastic!

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.780
Your mom's a great cook, isn't she?

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:36.660
Really?

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.160
Well, I guess I'll tell her that...

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.710
Oh yeah, about the groups for the summer camp...

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.340
Can I hand in a form with the four of us?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.180
Sounds good!

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.550
Yup!

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.970
This will be my first time on a trip with my friends!

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.470
I'm looking forward to it so much!

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:00.730
Right, Himawari?

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.730
Um... I guess.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.860
We'll swim in the sea,

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:07.690
build sand castles on the beach,

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.570
cook curry together...

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.650
Then don't forget about fireworks and a test of courage!

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.990
Oh, I wanna try watermelon splitting too!

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.830
I doubt we he have enough time...

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.870
Aw, really?

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:32.590
Hey Wakaba, who's she?

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.890
Ah, Kuroki?

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:37.390
She's Kuroki Rei.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.390
She's always by herself, isn't she?

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:43.560
I've seen her a bunch of times with my camera,

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.110
but I've never seen her talk outside of class.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.400
Can I ask you girls a favor?

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.410
Hey, Kuroki!

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:57.160
Have you joined a group for the summer camp yet?

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.290
No.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:02.040
Then would you like to join our group?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.250
I'm sure it'll be fun if we're all together.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.210
I'm fine by myself.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:13.840
What were you doing earlier this morning?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.260
Do you like bird-watching?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:18.640
I don't know what you mean.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.560
What a weirdo.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:28.650
This is the data we've gathered about the transformations

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.200
and power surges of the four Alones that have emerged so far.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:35.280
We attempted an analysis from all possible viewpoints,

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.120
but we couldn't find any systematic patterns.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.080
I wonder if it's just a self-defense mechanism they have.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:43.960
Wait a moment!

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.550
Scroll back 12 milliseconds on the fourth manifest waveform sensor!

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.760
Right away.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.930
Look at that! That's it!

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.760
It's clear proof of external interference!

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:01.770
No way... So there is a third party involved in the Alone attacks?

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.160
Will our home be okay?

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.170
There won't be any more scary monsters, right?

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.420
How should I know?

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.050
Let's get going.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:37.350
Watch out!

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.780
Th-Thank you...

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.450
That was so scary...

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.330
So cool!

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.470
I'm home, Piisuke.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:20.270
Good morning!

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.480
You should say "welcome home", not "good morning."

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.190
Good morning! Good morning!

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:27.480
Guess what, Piisuke?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:32.200
I saw a really pretty white flower on the way to school.

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.570
I looked it up and learned it's called a fishwort.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.240
It's such an ugly name for a cute flower.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.420
Oh yeah, I also heard some cuckoos cry.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:46.420
It's almost the season they look for a mate.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.960
Also—

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.470
What's wrong, Piisuke?

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.520
Bear with me for a moment.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.770
<i>Welcome home, Rei.</i>

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.820
What do you want?

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.740
<i>I saw you save a child.</i>

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:14.990
<i>You promised to not interfere.</i>

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:16.280
I was just—

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.250
<i>I see you're still uncertain.</i>

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.080
<i>This world must face destruction.</i>

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:31.800
<i>It is your heart and your heart alone which transforms the Alone.</i>

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:37.640
<i>The stronger your desire, the stronger they are reborn.</i>

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.060
<i>And yet!</i>

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.600
I'm not uncertain!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.190
<i>They will not give you an infinite number of chances.</i>

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:49.820
<i>You must never forget your duty, even for a moment.</i>

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:54.740
<i>It is for the sake of your fallen world.</i>

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.230
Seven more...

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:40.160
My duty is to destroy the Manifestor Engine...

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.790
But I don't need the Alones to do that...

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.580
A security robot?!

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.250
How long have they had these?

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.980
Vroom, vroom, vroom-r-room...

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:29.530
All day, every day, vroom-vroom with Dogg—

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:30.030
Hmm?

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:45.580
Kuroki!

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.640
<i>I'm home!</i>

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.980
<i>Mom? Dad?</i>

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:10.320
<i>Rei!</i>

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.280
<i>Mom?</i>

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:12.740
<i>Rei!</i>

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:13.990
<i>Dad?</i>

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.490
<i>No!</i>

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:25.250
Ouch!

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:27.750
Stop right there!

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:31.590
The doctor said you gotta rest for at least a day!

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.140
You still got a bit of a fever.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.650
But it's way better than it was yesterday though.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:44.520
Where am I?

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:46.110
My place.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.320
I'm the only one home today, so don't worry about formalities.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:52.240
Oh right, are you hungry?

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:53.400
I prepared some rice porridge.

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:55.910
I'm fine...

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.040
Wait a moment. I'll bring you some right away.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.230
Say "ah"!

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:24.230
I can eat on my own.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.060
Really?

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.360
Okay then.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.860
How is it? Is it yummy?

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:35.870
It's good.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.450
I know, right?

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:42.000
Though it was my little sister, Momo, who made it.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.250
You really surprised me, you know!

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.050
You were just lying there on the beach passed out!

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.380
I wouldn't have noticed you if the seagulls didn't show me.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.840
What were you doing out there?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:13:59.640
Taking a walk.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.140
Hey, Rei!

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.150
I can call you Rei, right?

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:12.150
Whatever.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:13.400
Hurray!

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.360
Yay!

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:18.530
Then call me Akane, okay?

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:25.670
It isn't working.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:30.170
It's too heavily damaged to retrieve any image data from it.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:35.760
I originally designed them to be disposable, single-purpose machines.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:39.180
I guess using them as guards was a bit too much.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:42.350
Dr. Isshiki!

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.900
We've detected something that might be an Alone near Ogasawara.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.310
What?!

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.770
Oh, by the way,

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.570
you should tell your family that you're here.

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:53.910
Wanna use the phone?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.490
It's okay.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.990
They're somewhere far away, where phones can't reach.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.250
Really?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.370
You must miss them.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:09.300
What about your parents?

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:15.390
My dad died in an accident when I was seven.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:20.170
My mom's been hospitalized in Atami since then too.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:25.480
But I've got my little sister and grandpa, so I'm not lonely at all!

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.400
I have my friends too!

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.610
May I ask you something?

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.030
Sure, what?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.620
If you could get your dad back...

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.120
If your mom could leave the hospital...

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.380
Would you do whatever it takes?

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.540
Yeah!

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:49.880
I'd do all I could!

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:56.550
Well, I wouldn't want to cause trouble to my friends and other people.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.020
"Respect people."

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.270
"Treasure your friends."

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:05.650
My parents always told me that.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:07.820
They wouldn't be happy if I brought them back

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.030
if it meant that I had to trouble others.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.610
My key!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.030
No way! Where is it?

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.200
What's wrong, Rei?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.870
My key! My key's gone!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:21.370
What key?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.130
Stop! You gotta stay in bed!

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.590
Let me go! It's all I've got!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.140
I'm sorry.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:39.850
I'll be fine.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.270
Answer your phone.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:42.020
But...

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:46.060
Just leave me alone for a moment please...

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.820
Ms. Mizuho? Yes.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.030
I know you're there.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.040
<i>Then why are you lazing around?</i>

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.540
<i>It's your moment to act.</i>

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.670
What? An Alone?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.930
I'm on my way.

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:12.010
I'm sorry, Rei, but I've gotta go out for a little!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.590
Be sure to stay in bed, okay? Promise!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:25.190
Mizuho, where are the girls?!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.560
They should arrive at the target any moment.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.370
Girls!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.780
Ignition!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.670
Texture on!

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.150
<i>Dad?</i>

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.110
<i>Mom?</i>

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.110
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:12.360
<i>The Manifestor's energy became critical and had a meltdown.</i>

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:19.870
<i>Because of that, your parents, friends, and entire world was destroyed.</i>

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:23.120
<i>Destroyed?</i>

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:29.210
<i>Fate chose to end your world.</i>

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:33.090
<i>But if you desire to change this fate,</i>

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.640
they<i> are willing to help.</i>

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.390
<i>They?</i>

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.730
<i>They are the ones who dwell on the borderline between the beginning and the end.</i>

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:46.360
<i>They have the ability to regenerate your world.</i>

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:48.860
<i>Please return everything to how it was!</i>

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.280
<i>Let me see everyone again!</i>

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.780
<i>However, there is one condition...</i>

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.700
<i>A condition?</i>

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.720
I... must do this...

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.680
I... decided...

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.060
So please...

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:22.640
Don't get in the way...

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.120
I failed again...

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.090
My key...

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.590
Hey!

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.800
Good morning!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:58.810
Is your fever down?

00:20:01.270 --> 00:20:03.060
Looks like you're fine.

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:07.400
Jeez! I told you to stay in bed!

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:09.480
What were you doing out there?

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:13.530
I saw that another monster appeared.

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:16.990
Uh, d-don't worry about that!

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:20.540
The... navy dealt with it!

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.250
I see.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.290
Um... Where was it?

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:29.800
I figured it might be at the beach where I found you,

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:35.590
so I asked Aoi, Wakaba, and Himawari to help me look for it yesterday.

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:42.980
This is the key to my old house.

00:20:42.980 --> 00:20:45.860
It's full of my dearest memories.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:48.860
I see. I'm glad we found it then!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:52.740
Hey, Rei!

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:56.740
You should join our group for the summer camp!

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:01.450
The girls and I all wanna become friends with you!

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:02.120
Sound good?

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:06.250
I'm really grateful for the key.

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:12.260
But don't be so nice to me anymore...

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.290
Hey, Mom!

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.450
Hello!

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.250
Momo fell asleep?

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:47.000
She said she'd wait for you, but she didn't hold up for long.

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:50.840
So? Has your friend gotten better?

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:52.510
Yeah,

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:54.260
but...

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:57.260
Come here, Akane.

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:58.850
Mom...

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:06.900
I asked her to be my friend,

00:22:06.900 --> 00:22:08.770
but she refused...

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:10.030
I see...

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:14.990
Do you no longer want to become friends with her?

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:20.830
Then don't give up and keep reaching out to her.

00:22:20.830 --> 00:22:23.750
As long as you never forget the love in your heart,

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:27.000
I'm sure you'll reach out to her one day.

00:22:29.500 --> 00:22:31.550
That's not fair, Akane!

00:22:31.840 --> 00:22:33.680
Me too!

00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:35.470
Okay, come on, Momo!

00:24:13.860 --> 00:24:15.200
Vroom-r-room...

00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:16.450
Isshiki Akane here!

00:24:16.450 --> 00:24:18.000
Summer school starts next week!

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.240
I wonder what exciting things await.

00:24:19.240 --> 00:24:21.000
Next time: The Story of How Kenjiro Tries

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.000
to Strengthen Everyone's Friendship Power,

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:25.460
but Something Terrible Happens.

00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:26.540
It's gonna be great!
